# glm-prepare-host.patch (sync, 2026-10-29; no production counterpart): a chat request's preparation (GlmApp._prepare)
# on the synced base had upstream costs production never had; they are cut with the same prompt ids:
#  - the kept reasoning was walked twice: _messages_to_mask restores it before the literal mask (recipe 0116), then the
#    template restored again and found nothing more (a filled step carries reasoning, which restore skips; an unfilled
#    one has the same keys again, the conversation's hash leaving reasoning out). _messages_to_mask now returns
#    app.Restored, which the template takes as it is; a masked copy is a plain list and is restored as before;
#  - the literal mask scanned every string twice: for a mask character, then for guarded text through an alternation
#    of the 35 guarded texts tried one by one. Now one walk (literal_tokens._strings) passes every string an earlier
#    request showed holds nothing to mask (LiteralTokens._clean: an agent's turn sends its whole history again, so a
#    dict lookup - the string's hash, then its characters compared - replaces both scans; at most CLEAN_CHARS
#    characters, the oldest out first), matches guarded text through a prefix trie (literal_tokens._trie; _find stays
#    the substitution's), and skips the mask-character scan for an ASCII string, which cannot hold one.
# Measured on test_prompt_ids.py F's ~671k-token agent turn, each request a fresh JSON object as a server parses it
# (workstation CPU, median of five): _prepare 83.4 -> 52.5 ms; production, which has neither cost, 51.9 ms.
# Test: tests/host/test_prepare_once.py (restore once, the same render; the trie and _maybe against the alternation;
# _collides against the class; _strings against _any_string; mask with the memory against a reference copy of the
# code before the patch over 600 requests, the memory clean and bounded; _prepare's prompt ids with and without the
# shortcuts); mutants: tests/host/mutants_prepare_once.py (10 of 10 killed). Applies after
# glm-prestage-one-array.patch.
